      "writtenOn": "2021-05-12T16:06:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I realized that I broke some tests. I forgot that when a test panics that it aborts processing of all tests in that package so I just fixed what I thought was the only test failure and uploaded but there were other failures.\n\nSome of those other failing tests seem related to this issue. Although I can\u0027t quite see how the lack of a platform variant is changing the behavior of the version mutators.\n\nIt seems to me that we are overloading \"platform variant\" to mean a number of different things:\n1. An actual different variant of the module that becomes part of the platform.\n2. The stubs for a module that is part of an APEX and is used by the platform but is not itself part of the platform.\n3. To make a module usable from within make.\n\nSo, a module that is part of an APEX and provides stubs cannot also be part of the platform. Which is probably a good thing but it is a little confusing.\n\nI will take a look and see if I can fix this.",
      "parentUuid": "400d3419_53740af7",
      "revId": "a3378371dcb4d0e146116534b31152441fe7a16d",
